    def longestPalindrome(self, s: str) -> str:
        start, length = 0, 0
        for i in range(len(s)):
            for l, r in ((i, i), (i, i + 1)):  # odd centre, even centre
                while l >= 0 and r < len(s) and s[l] == s[r]:
                    l -= 1
                    r += 1
                if r - l - 1 > length:
                    start, length = l + 1, r - l - 1
        return s[start:start + length]
```

**Time:** O(n²): n centres, each expansion up to n
**Space:** O(1)
:::

:::details 2. DP table
`pal[i][j]` is true when `s[i] == s[j]` and the inside `s[i+1..j−1]` is a palindrome (or has length < 2). Fill by increasing `i` from the right so `pal[i+1][j−1]` is ready.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public String longestPalindrome(String s) {
        int n = s.length(), start = 0, len = 1;
        boolean[][] pal = new boolean[n][n];
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                pal[i][j] = s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j) && (j - i < 2 || pal[i + 1][j - 1]);
                if (pal[i][j] && j - i + 1 > len) { len = j - i + 1; start = i; }
            }
        return s.substring(start, start + len);
    }
}
```

