:::details 3. Manacher's algorithm
Compute the palindrome radius `p[i]` at every centre of the `#`-padded string in linear time (see Longest Palindromic Substring). A centre with radius `p` contributes `(p + 1) / 2` palindromes of the original string.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int countSubstrings(String s) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("^");
        for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) sb.append('#').append(ch);
        char[] t = sb.append("#$").toString().toCharArray();
        int[] p = new int[t.length];
        int center = 0, right = 0, count = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i < t.length - 1; i++) {
            if (i < right) p[i] = Math.min(right - i, p[2 * center - i]);
            while (t[i + p[i] + 1] == t[i - p[i] - 1]) p[i]++;
            if (i + p[i] > right) { center = i; right = i + p[i]; }
            count += (p[i] + 1) / 2;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

