**Pattern:** Linear sweep (before / overlap / after)

**Key insight:** Copy intervals ending before it, absorb all overlapping ones into it, then copy the rest.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int[][] insert(int[][] intervals, int[] nw) {
        List<int[]> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int i = 0, n = intervals.length;
        while (i < n && intervals[i][1] < nw[0]) res.add(intervals[i++]);
        int lo = nw[0], hi = nw[1];
        while (i < n && intervals[i][0] <= hi) {
            lo = Math.min(lo, intervals[i][0]);
            hi = Math.max(hi, intervals[i][1]);
            i++;
        }
        res.add(new int[]{lo, hi});
        while (i < n) res.add(intervals[i++]);
        return res.toArray(new int[0][]);
    }
}
```

