**Pattern:** Sweep over sorted starts and ends

**Key insight:** Two sorted arrays: a start before the earliest unfinished end needs a new room.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {
        int n = intervals.length;
        int[] s = new int[n], e = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { s[i] = intervals[i][0]; e[i] = intervals[i][1]; }
        Arrays.sort(s);
        Arrays.sort(e);
        int rooms = 0, j = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (s[i] < e[j]) rooms++;
            else j++;
        }
        return rooms;
    }
}
